# Read by `semgrep scan` from the repository root, so it applies to the
# security gate's command, which takes no --exclude of its own. A
# .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in ignore list rather than adding to
# it, so that list is repeated first, unchanged.

# Semgrep's defaults: common large paths.
node_modules/
build/
dist/
vendor/
.env/
.venv/
.tox/
*.min.js
.npm/
.yarn/

# Semgrep's defaults: common test paths.
test/
tests/
*_test.go

# Semgrep's defaults: its rules and log folders.
.semgrep
.semgrep_logs/

# This repository: every testdata/ directory holds synthetic fixtures, source
# written to misuse a client (raw SQL, an unverified TLS context, a sleep in a
# retry loop) so rvl's scan has something to detect. A finding there is the
# fixture working. Out of scope per SECURITY.md.
testdata/
